1
00:00:58,399 --> 00:00:59,560
Let me tell you right now,

2
00:01:00,679 --> 00:01:02,159
I'm just a cuckold!

3
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:05,120
They got married. Got the license and everything.

4
00:01:07,879 --> 00:01:08,799
Calm down.

5
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:10,799
Listen to me.

6
00:01:11,719 --> 00:01:12,519
Bro.

7
00:01:13,599 --> 00:01:14,599
Take my advice.

8
00:01:14,599 --> 00:01:15,200
Okay?

9
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:16,560
It's really not worth it.

10
00:01:17,959 --> 00:01:19,599
Take a step back and let it go.

11
00:01:20,959 --> 00:01:21,760
Step back?

12
00:01:23,159 --> 00:01:24,560
Where am I supposed to step back to?

13
00:01:28,719 --> 00:01:31,159
They've already gotten their marriage license.

14
00:01:31,359 --> 00:01:32,480
Wait, wait, wait.

15
00:01:33,359 --> 00:01:34,239
They got a marriage license?

16
00:01:34,239 --> 00:01:35,519
Did you divorce her?

17
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:38,920
I never even had a marriage license!

18
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:40,640
That bitch said,

19
00:01:40,879 --> 00:01:42,079
without an apartment,

20
00:01:42,079 --> 00:01:43,920
without our own assets,

21
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,400
and without a bride price,

22
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,840
she wouldn't marry me!

23
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,640
Stop yelling. Being loud doesn't make you right.

24
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:49,640
I'm telling you right now,

25
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:51,239
from a legal standpoint,

26
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:53,159
they are legally married.

27
00:01:53,159 --> 00:01:53,959
Understand?

28
00:01:55,079 --> 00:01:56,359
You legal illiterate.

29
00:01:57,959 --> 00:01:58,879
Can I kill him?

30
00:02:00,319 --> 00:02:01,879
So childish. Seriously so childish.

31
00:02:02,799 --> 00:02:03,599
I'll kill him.

32
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,640
Why are you acting like a psycho?

33
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:06,000
I'll kill him!

34
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:06,680
I'll kill him!

35
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:07,920
Killing him is against the law!

36
00:02:08,039 --> 00:02:09,840
It's not like you don't watch movies or TV.

37
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,319
In those films of Hong Kong, China...

38
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:12,080
Shut up!

39
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,319
That's so suffocating!

40
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:17,120
Have you been watching too many movies from Hong Kong, China, and Taiwan?

41
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:19,080
My rule is,

42
00:02:19,759 --> 00:02:23,039
first beat that bitch till she's crippled,

43
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,479
and then

44
00:02:27,639 --> 00:02:29,080
kill the adulterer!

45
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,000
Let me tell you once more,

46
00:02:31,319 --> 00:02:33,639
there must be someone else.

47
00:02:33,759 --> 00:02:35,240
More than one.

48
00:02:36,599 --> 00:02:37,520
As for this mess,

49
00:02:37,719 --> 00:02:39,000
once I find out who,

50
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:41,159
I'll slaughter them!

51
00:02:41,439 --> 00:02:42,240
Bro.

52
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,639
Listen to me, okay?

53
00:02:43,639 --> 00:02:44,639
Just one thing.

54
00:02:44,759 --> 00:02:45,479
Speak.

55
00:02:45,479 --> 00:02:47,120
This whole thing can be big or small.

56
00:02:48,639 --> 00:02:49,560
I admit,

57
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:52,199
she might have crossed the line before.

58
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,120
Crossed the line?

59
00:02:53,639 --> 00:02:54,560
That's not crossing the line!

60
00:02:54,879 --> 00:02:56,439
Call it what it is: she's a slut!

61
00:02:57,919 --> 00:02:58,520
Go on.

62
00:02:58,759 --> 00:02:59,800
Still, you shouldn't

63
00:03:00,199 --> 00:03:01,439
hang yourself on one tree.

64
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,639
I won't hang!

65
00:03:02,639 --> 00:03:03,639
This isn't the old society anymore.

66
00:03:03,639 --> 00:03:04,520
We live in a society of laws.

67
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,599
Think about it carefully.

68
00:03:05,759 --> 00:03:07,520
If you kill someone, you pay with your life!

69
00:03:07,759 --> 00:03:09,199
Murder means paying with your life!

70
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:10,879
You can't throw your life away

71
00:03:10,879 --> 00:03:12,280
over some stupid bullshit like this!

72
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:12,960
Is it worth it?

73
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,719
Tell me, is it worth it?

74
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:20,599
There's no other way.

75
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,919
I've already made up my mind.

76
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,919
I have one last favor to ask.

77
00:03:30,759 --> 00:03:31,520
Tomorrow,

78
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:35,840
come with me to see that guy named Liangzi.

79
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,280
Don't look panicked.

80
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,159
I...

81
00:03:51,039 --> 00:03:51,840
Are you coming or not?

82
00:03:57,319 --> 00:03:58,680
What are you crying for?

83
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,560
Why?

84
00:04:10,719 --> 00:04:13,080
Remember: better to die on your feet

85
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:14,719
than to perish on your knees.

86
00:04:15,319 --> 00:04:16,079
A man

87
00:04:16,879 --> 00:04:18,480
lives for his hide,

88
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:22,120
a tree lives for its face!

89
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,959
You got it backwards, you fool.

90
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,240
Whatever.

91
00:04:27,399 --> 00:04:28,959
They're both the outer layer anyway.

92
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:30,680
Are you coming or not?

93
00:04:50,439 --> 00:04:51,079
Bro.

94
00:04:51,839 --> 00:04:52,399
Come here.

95
00:04:56,959 --> 00:04:57,759
Liangzi.

96
00:04:58,519 --> 00:04:59,480
You still dare to show up?

97
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,639
Haven't had enough beatings?

98
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:02,560
No, no.

99
00:05:02,839 --> 00:05:03,639
Not at all.

100
00:05:03,839 --> 00:05:05,000
Talk straight.

101
00:05:05,759 --> 00:05:06,800
Wipe that smirk off your face.

102
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,040
I've thought it over.

103
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,000
That bitch...

104
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:16,639
Who's a bitch?

105
00:05:18,199 --> 00:05:18,920
I mean...

106
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,879
Don't you know we got married?

107
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,000
Are you here to give wedding cash?

108
00:05:30,439 --> 00:05:31,120
Liangzi...

109
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:33,360
Then I gotta congratulate you.

110
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,480
Congratulations, congratulations.

111
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:41,240
I...

112
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,120
wanted to discuss something with you.

113
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:43,920
Out with it.

114
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,680
Could you maybe spare a little compensation?

115
00:05:48,839 --> 00:05:49,480
Not much.

116
00:05:51,639 --> 00:05:52,240
5,000.

117
00:06:11,959 --> 00:06:12,759
5,000.

118
00:06:15,399 --> 00:06:16,240
Here, brother.

119
00:06:16,519 --> 00:06:17,160
Here.

120
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,120
Have a smoke.

121
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,279
You...

122
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:21,720
are a real man.

123
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,759
I had this ready for you.

124
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:27,399
It's only 5,000, right?

125
00:06:29,959 --> 00:06:30,399
10,000.

126
00:06:30,519 --> 00:06:31,079
Take it.

127
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:32,680
From now on,

128
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:34,000
we're not just brothers,

129
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,600
we're family.

130
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,160
Closer than ever.

131
00:06:41,439 --> 00:06:42,240
Thanks.

132
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:51,600
Take care.

133
00:06:53,319 --> 00:06:54,839
Your cousin's quite a character.

134
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:15,120
Within three days,

135
00:07:16,759 --> 00:07:17,920
get me a piece.

136
00:07:18,199 --> 00:07:20,000
Bro, you've really lost your mind.

137
00:07:20,319 --> 00:07:22,319
Aunt can take it, Uncle can't!

138
00:07:22,399 --> 00:07:24,079
If this can be tolerated, what can't?

139
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:25,600
Alright, alright, alright.

140
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,680
Forget who can take what!

141
00:07:27,959 --> 00:07:29,399
Calling me brainless?

142
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,319
We take the cash he gave us,

143
00:07:32,199 --> 00:07:33,199
buy a piece,

144
00:07:33,639 --> 00:07:34,959
and then I'll take him out.

145
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:36,519
Bro,

146
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:39,639
tell me, ain't that genius?

147
00:07:45,639 --> 00:07:46,639
I'll wait to hear from you.

148
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:56,839
Where'd that money come from?

149
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:00,240
That brother gave it to me.

150
00:08:03,639 --> 00:08:04,519
You've got to understand,

151
00:08:04,959 --> 00:08:05,879
I'm not after your money,

152
00:08:05,879 --> 00:08:06,959
or out for any gain.

153
00:08:06,959 --> 00:08:08,639
You're not like everyone else to me.

154
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,720
I just really care about you, little bro.

155
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:11,480
Got it.

156
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:12,920
Sis,

157
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,720
let me get you some water.

158
00:08:26,199 --> 00:08:27,319
Here's some water, Sis.

159
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:36,000
I know who's genuinely good to me.

160
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,759
Your brother might look big and tough,

161
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:41,279
but he's as petty as they come.

162
00:08:42,759 --> 00:08:43,759
Like he'd ever back down.

163
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,600
Sis, I'll tell you everything.

164
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:49,120
My brother told me to get him a gun.

165
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,039
Gave me three days.

166
00:08:51,399 --> 00:08:52,840
No way I'm doing that.

167
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,360
Wait for my word.

168
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:04,559
I'll handle it.

169
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:15,200
What's there to handle?

170
00:09:30,639 --> 00:09:31,840
Drinking again, huh?

171
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,320
I came to thank you.

172
00:09:38,399 --> 00:09:39,240
Thank me for what?

173
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:39,919
I'm your brother.

174
00:09:49,039 --> 00:09:49,720
What's this...

175
00:09:50,679 --> 00:09:51,679
Where'd you get this, bro?

176
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,360
Put it away.

177
00:09:55,159 --> 00:09:55,960
Where'd it come from?

178
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:57,720
Quit playing dumb.

179
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,240
Didn't you give it to me?

180
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:00,200
Bought it for me.

181
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,519
Left it at my place.

182
00:10:02,559 --> 00:10:03,480
The house key...

183
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,000
you're the only one with a copy.

184
00:10:05,919 --> 00:10:07,360
I sure as hell didn't buy it for you.

185
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:09,279
Bro...

186
00:10:10,279 --> 00:10:11,120
Buying a gun is illegal.

187
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:12,080
Murder gets you the death penalty.

188
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:12,919
We have to turn it in.

189
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,440
Turn it in right now.

190
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,279
That Liang bastard...

191
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:19,039
he won't let this go.

192
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:21,519
Right now,

193
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:24,000
I can't worry about all that.

194
00:10:25,679 --> 00:10:27,039
No, we have laws now.

195
00:10:27,039 --> 00:10:27,919
Call the cops.

196
00:10:27,919 --> 00:10:29,399
Why can't you just call the cops?

197
00:10:30,519 --> 00:10:31,720
I'm a real man.

198
00:10:32,159 --> 00:10:33,799
I have my dignity!

199
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:34,960
Call the cops?

200
00:10:36,759 --> 00:10:37,960
He slept with my wife,

201
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,679
and now he wants to screw me over too!

202
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,120
Hold on...

203
00:10:43,399 --> 00:10:44,279
You're my brother.

204
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:45,399
Are you my brother or not?

205
00:10:46,399 --> 00:10:47,799
How much did you drink?

206
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,799
They're legally married!

207
00:10:50,799 --> 00:10:52,120
They got a marriage license!

208
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:55,919
Come on.

209
00:11:01,759 --> 00:11:02,559
Put it away.

210
00:11:02,679 --> 00:11:03,559
That's enough, brother.

211
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:10,039
You're the closest person to me.

212
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,039
I came to say goodbye.

213
00:11:13,879 --> 00:11:14,759
Take care of yourself.

214
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:16,039
Listen to me.

215
00:11:16,039 --> 00:11:17,360
You've lost your mind.

216
00:11:17,559 --> 00:11:18,320
You're talking crazy.

217
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:19,679
I didn't give you this gun.

218
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:21,200
Then my sister-in-law gave it to you.

219
00:11:21,519 --> 00:11:23,240
Then think about who gave it to her!

220
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,679
Maybe it was Liangzi!

221
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,320
It's a trap!

222
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,240
Even if it's a trap,

223
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:31,480
I still have to jump in.

224
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:36,200
This thing...

225
00:11:38,399 --> 00:11:40,080
I tested it where nobody was around.

226
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:43,440
A real piece.

227
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,440
Where did you test it?

228
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,639
Tell me where you tested it!

229
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:53,960
They can trace that!

230
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:57,240
Worst case,

231
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,279
we take each other down!

232
00:12:02,919 --> 00:12:05,159
I'm not changing my mind!

233
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,279
That's a real gun!

234
00:12:07,519 --> 00:12:09,080
Where did you fire those shots?

235
00:12:09,399 --> 00:12:11,240
Ballistics can trace everything these days!

236
00:12:28,879 --> 00:12:29,159
Sis,

237
00:12:29,159 --> 00:12:30,200
you put on quite an act.

238
00:12:35,519 --> 00:12:36,519
Isn't this perfect?

239
00:12:36,799 --> 00:12:38,159
No matter who kills who,

240
00:12:38,279 --> 00:12:39,120
the other gets executed.

241
00:12:39,399 --> 00:12:40,559
Then we can be together.

242
00:12:42,639 --> 00:12:44,679
Wait, why is everything so messed up?

243
00:12:45,559 --> 00:12:47,799
Sis, what's the deal with the gun?

244
00:12:48,039 --> 00:12:48,879
Liangzi gave it to me.

245
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,440
He wanted your brother to walk right into it.

246
00:12:52,519 --> 00:12:53,799
You know what your brother's like.

247
00:12:53,799 --> 00:12:55,039
A drink or two, and he loses his mind.

248
00:12:55,159 --> 00:12:56,279
All he knows is brute force.

249
00:12:58,279 --> 00:12:59,840
His bullets were fake.

250
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,120
Sis...

251
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,919
They were real, Sis.

252
00:13:02,919 --> 00:13:03,679
Yeah.

253
00:13:03,679 --> 00:13:04,759
He fired two shots.

254
00:13:04,919 --> 00:13:05,919
I know.

255
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,360
I swapped them for real ones!

256
00:13:08,159 --> 00:13:10,039
Don't worry, Liangzi loves hunting.

257
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:11,320
There are plenty of bullets in there.

258
00:13:12,039 --> 00:13:13,559
Wasn't this all your plan?

259
00:13:13,759 --> 00:13:15,600
What do you mean, my plan?

260
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:21,279
Xiao Guan,

261
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,679
you chicken out when things get real?

262
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:29,919
That night,

263
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:32,080
you knew your brother and I weren't married.

264
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:33,960
It was your idea

265
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:35,080
to introduce Liangzi to me,

266
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:35,960
told me to seduce him,

267
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:36,879
marry him,

268
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:39,240
and set your brother up to kill him.

269
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,200
That way,

270
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,639
the whole mine belongs to us.

271
00:13:41,639 --> 00:13:43,519
We'd be set for life!

272
00:13:44,639 --> 00:13:46,840
What did you call this move?

273
00:13:47,679 --> 00:13:49,279
The oriole behind.

274
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,039
Brilliant.

275
00:13:54,559 --> 00:13:55,960
Truly brilliant.

276
00:13:56,399 --> 00:13:57,600
I knew I wasn't wrong about you.

277
00:14:02,559 --> 00:14:03,519
Looking at you now...

278
00:14:04,679 --> 00:14:05,639
Think about it.

279
00:14:18,679 --> 00:14:19,360
Bro,

280
00:14:21,519 --> 00:14:22,840
once you finish *First Blood*,

281
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:23,720
you got *Second Blood*, right?

282
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:24,639
We'll talk about that later.

283
00:14:24,759 --> 00:14:25,600
Let me borrow your motorcycle.

284
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:26,559
I gotta head out in a rush.

285
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,039
The keys are in it.

286
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:29,879
Got it.

287
00:14:30,519 --> 00:14:32,039
Watch the shop for me. Thanks.

288
00:15:40,559 --> 00:15:41,399
Two of you,

289
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:43,399
take these two bastards,

290
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:45,200
toss them into the kiln,

291
00:15:45,639 --> 00:15:46,559
and burn them.

292
00:16:21,639 --> 00:16:22,639
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

293
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:23,320
Hurry!

294
00:17:01,919 --> 00:17:03,879
They say if you take dirt from under this old tree

295
00:17:03,919 --> 00:17:06,079
and put it in a wishing bottle, your wish comes true.

296
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:07,400
What did you wish for?

297
00:17:08,759 --> 00:17:10,440
I just want to hurry and graduate,

298
00:17:10,759 --> 00:17:12,559
then get a job in the big city.

299
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:14,880
My parents worked so hard.

300
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:16,519
I want to bring them to live with me.

301
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,559
You're so good to your parents.

302
00:17:19,559 --> 00:17:20,319
Thinking ahead, too.

303
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:21,839
All I want after graduation

304
00:17:21,839 --> 00:17:23,079
is to marry my partner right away,

305
00:17:23,079 --> 00:17:24,160
get a good job,

306
00:17:24,279 --> 00:17:25,519
and live a peaceful, stable life.

307
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:26,880
That's nice.

308
00:17:33,759 --> 00:17:34,359
Let's go.

309
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:36,720
Let's go.

310
00:17:40,799 --> 00:17:41,279
Come on.

311
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:08,160
I'm heading out then. Bye.

312
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:08,799
Talk soon.

313
00:18:08,799 --> 00:18:09,680
Get home safe.
